            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Well, I am an actual Mainer, and I thought this was an excellant base for Lobster Stew. Here's the trick to give it more flavor: first, make the stew the night before, as it will intensify greatly over night. Secondly, most restaurants add half a bottle or so of clam juice to their stew. This really brings out the lobster flavor. Again, this is a great base for classic lobster stew.... coming from a MAINER (born and raised)."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "amcc"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As others have said this is the quintessential New England Lobster Stew. However, there is a step missing in the instructions. Warm the cream before drizzling into the lobster and butter. Have made this with fat free half and half and Lactaid to suit diets and it always comes out great.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-30T21:27:57.422Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LABSARE4ME"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Marion, thanks for the real recipe. I too am from coastal Maine but I add one thing to this basic recipe. When picking out the lobsters I save the roe and tomalley. I first saute the roe and tomalley with butter and then add the lobster. It adds a deeper richness to the stew. I also agree, make it at least a day ahead of time for best flavor.\r\n:)",
            "datePublished": "2004-12-22T05:26:24.403Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DaringPlum4788"
            },
            "reviewBody": "When I buy my fresh lobster from the lobster pound I have them cook the lobsters for me so all I have to do is shuck them.",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-02T18:05:54.977Z"
          },
          {
